# CAPTURE: while a track plays, the keys on ARP or REC are kept (the last 32 notes, quantised like REC, with their held
# lengths). SAVE then REC writes them into the clip on screen and saves it. Keys played while stopped are not kept.
tapkey b9
expect trk 9
expect nsteps 0
tap ARP
tap PLAY
waitpos 9 2
wait 20
holdkey 12 300
waitpos 9 4
wait 20
holdkey 14 480
tap PLAY
tapkey 15
expect nsteps 0
# SAVE shows the pick with REC in it; REC saves the capture: the two notes, at their steps (a drum keeps its length)
tap SAVE
shot capture_pick.png
tap REC
expect view 4
expect stepon 2
expect stepon 4
expect nsteps 2
expectstep 2 65 3 3
expectstep 4 67 3 3
expect dirty 0
# a synth keeps the length each key was held: 300 ms = 10 quarter steps, 480 ms = 16 (at 125 BPM)
tap SEQ
tapkey b5
expect trk 5
tap ARP
tap PLAY
waitpos 5 2
wait 20
holdkey 12 300
waitpos 5 4
wait 20
holdkey 14 480
tap PLAY
tap SAVE
tap REC
expectstep 2 65 9 11
expectstep 4 67 15 18
expect dirty 0
